/-! # The thin Stage5b and Stage6 items through the hybrid checks (generated)

Generated. The 14 items proved with sloped secants in
`BccSharp.Cover.Stage5bPhaseLeaves` and `BccSharp.Cover.Stage6FLeaves` are passed through the hybrid
checks of `BccSharp.Cover.Stage3Stage6Hybrid`. Where the Adaptive proposal
is forecast to pass, the item has a hint. For Stage5b items the kernel
checks the hybrid check on the hint (`_hybrid`, `decide +kernel`), and the check stops
there. For Stage6 entries the kernel checks the hint (`entryN_hint`, `decide +kernel`), and
`entryN_hybrid` follows by `simp`. Elsewhere the hybrid check has no hint and falls back
to the box-built check; that `_hybrid` is derived from the existing `_check` theorem with
no new evaluation. Each theorem uses its own constant hint function and record number 0.
In the cover the hints are keyed by witness, so the Stage5b witnesses need distinct record
numbers. -/

